@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Simple SysML requirement graph — 3-4 «requirement» boxes + satisfy edge to a block.
'   usecase:      Teach requirement box (id/text), satisfy/verify/derive/trace.
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       systems-engineering
' ============================================================================
title Example SysML Requirement - Simple Satisfaction

' «requirement» is a SysML stereotype on Class. Inside: id and text properties.
' «satisfy»/«verify»/«deriveReqt»/«trace» are dependency stereotypes between
' requirements and other model elements (blocks, test cases).

' ---- Requirements ---------------------------------------------------------
class "Max Payload" <<requirement>> {
  id : REQ-001
  text : "The robot shall lift at least 5 kg."
}

class "Reach Distance" <<requirement>> {
  id : REQ-002
  text : "The robot shall reach 1.2 m horizontally."
}

class "Cycle Time" <<requirement>> {
  id : REQ-003
  text : "The robot shall complete a cycle in under 10 s."
}

' ---- Block that satisfies them -------------------------------------------
class "ArmController" <<block>> {
  payloadKg : 7
  reachM : 1.3
}

' ---- Dependency stereotypes ---------------------------------------------
' «satisfy» — a block/design realizes a requirement.
' «verify»  — a test case demonstrates compliance.
' «deriveReqt» — one requirement derived from another.
' «trace» — generic historical/auxiliary link.
class "PayloadBenchTest" <<testCase>> {
  id : TC-001
}

"ArmController" ..> "Max Payload" : <<satisfy>>
"ArmController" ..> "Reach Distance" : <<satisfy>>
"PayloadBenchTest" ..> "Max Payload" : <<verify>>

note bottom of "Max Payload"
  <b>Requirement box convention:</b>
  - id : the requirement identifier
  - text : the "shall" statement
  - Optional: source, verifyMethod,
    risk, status.
end note

@enduml
